# Step 1: Install WiX Toolset

    Download and install WiX Toolset from the WiX website.
    WiX Toolset is a collection of tools that allows you to create Windows Installer (MSI) packages.

    Install WiX extension for Visual Studio (if you're using Visual Studio):

    By default WiX is not included in Visual Studio, so you need to install the WiX Toolset Visual Studio Extension.
    search like this wiX toolset visual studio extension 2022/2019.. on google then Download and install.


   WiX supports adding .dll or project outputs as references (in .csproj format), not .exe files directly.BUT:

        You can still bundle your compiled .exe output and install it via WiX — you just have to manually include the file in your WiX setup.
      # Inside the <Directory> tag, you can manually add your .exe like this:
        <Directory Id="TARGETDIR" Name="SourceDir">
        <Directory Id="ProgramFilesFolder">
            <Directory Id="INSTALLFOLDER" Name="MyTrayApp">
            <Component Id="MyTrayAppExe" Guid="PUT-GUID-HERE">
                <File Source="..\MyTrayApp\bin\Release\net8.0-windows\MyTrayApp.exe" />
            </Component>
            </Directory>
        </Directory>
        </Directory>
